 ## Background
-GS-PS is a method for calibrated photometric stereo using 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on the Adaptive Spatio-Temporal 3D Gaussian Splatting method [9535-adaptive-spatio-temporal-3d-gaussian-splatting.md] by incorporating photometric and normal regularization losses [S1][S2, unofficial]. The baseline method compared against is Woodham [12] (1980) [S1][S2, unofficial]. The Gaussian Splatting base method is by Kerbl et al. [5] (2023) [S1][S2, unofficial].
+The method is based on the Gaussian Splatting base method by Kerbl et al. [5] (2023) [S1]. It revisits the problem of calibrated photometric stereo, originally addressed by Woodham [12] (1980) [S1]. The approach was developed to leverage the efficiency and explicit representation of 3D Gaussian Splatting for normal estimation [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
